{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>The sons of Levi.</b> And it does not say ״all,״ because not all of them were valiant men to do what was said in the matter. And one needs to know why it was necessary to mention them and did not rely on what their mention in the adjacent verse. And perhaps it comes to diminish — that the matter was not done with anyone other than them. And from the first verse, which said ״וַיֵּאָסְפוּ אֵלָיו כָּל בְּנֵי לֵוִי״, one should not infer that it excluded any Israelite; rather, it comes to say that all the sons of Levi came, and there is room to say that some from Israel also came. Therefore it says <b>וַיַּעֲשׂוּ בְנֵי לֵוִי</b> — to say, and not any Israelite." "<b>As Moses said.</b> Meaning, for the word of Moses alone sufficed for what they did to him. Or it further intends that they did not delay but as soon as he finished speaking — immediately upon the completion of his words they acted."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:13.833309801Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}